# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DateDrop — local environment
#
# Only the two Convex URLs live here. Every secret lives on the Convex
# deployment itself (`npx convex env set NAME value`) so it is never bundled
# into the browser and never lands in git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Written automatically by `npx convex dev`.
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:your-deployment-name
VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://your-deployment-name.convex.cloud
VITE_CONVEX_SITE_URL=https://your-deployment-name.convex.site


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set these ON THE CONVEX DEPLOYMENT, not in this file:
#
#   npx convex env set OPENAI_API_KEY sk-...
#     Required for real matching, ranking, venue extraction and plan writing.
#     Without it DateDrop falls back to deterministic extraction and planning,
#     and says so in the UI.
#
#   npx convex env set FIRECRAWL_API_KEY fc-...
#     Optional. /v2/search works unauthenticated at a lower rate limit;
#     /v2/scrape requires a key.
#
#   npx convex env set AGENTMAIL_API_KEY am_...
#   npx convex env set AGENTMAIL_INBOX_ID datedrop-concierge@agentmail.to
#   npx convex env set AGENTMAIL_WEBHOOK_SECRET whsec_...
#     Required to actually send and receive Concierge mail. Provision the
#     inbox and webhook with:
#       npx convex run setup:provisionAgentMail \
#         '{"webhookUrl":"https://<deployment>.convex.site/webhooks/agentmail"}'
#
#   npx convex env set SITE_URL https://<deployment>.convex.site
#     The public origin used in email links and by Convex Auth.
#
#   npx convex env set OPENAI_MODEL gpt-5.6-terra
#     Optional override for the head of the model ladder.
#
# Auth keys (JWT_PRIVATE_KEY, JWKS) are generated during setup — see README.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
